/*****************************************************************************
    jitXmutual -- MUTUAL RECURSION BETWEEN TWO KANT ACTIONS, UNDER JIT.
    2026-08-08. The second half of the genKantParse call measurement.

    WHY THIS AND NOT jitXcall ALONE. jitXcall proved an ACYCLIC call is emitted
    and runs at run time (ticks 2, 8 -> 22, one compile, degrade 0). That is
    not the shape genParse depends on. genParseSpec S2.6 rests explicitly on a
    CYCLIC call graph -- `JSONblock -> JSONfield -> JSONvalue -> JSONblock` --
    and argues it terminates because JSONblock consumes `{` before descending.
    A recursive-descent parser IS a cycle by construction, so if the emit walk
    cannot close a cycle, genKantParse has no jitted path for any real grammar.

    THE RIVAL IS NOT "wrong answer", IT IS "does not return". jitEmitSelfCall
    was built (2026-08-05, ladder rung JS) because a self-call inside an
    INLINED body replayed the enclosing preamble -- the pre-fix binary exits
    139 after 173,400 replays. Its cure is a map populated by an inline-stack
    test at discovery. THE QUESTION HERE IS WHETHER THAT TEST SEES A CYCLE OF
    LENGTH TWO, or only length one.

    RUN THIS UNDER A WALL-CLOCK CAP (H5). A non-terminating emit walk is not a
    wrong answer, it is the absence of a run, and it will take the terminal
    with it.

    jmTicks is a COUNT, and the counts are chosen non-equal across fires so a
    slot that merely defaults cannot pass (H4 / the anti-vacuity rule):
        fire 1  jmN = 4  ->  jmTicks 4
        fire 2  jmN = 6  ->  jmTicks 6   NO RECOMPILE

    DIAGNOSTIC:
        ticks 4 then 10 (4+6)   EMITTED, cycle closed, runs at run time
        ticks 4 then 4          the second fire ran nothing -- folded
        hang / 139              the emit walk cannot close a two-cycle
        degrade > 0             the cycle was declined rather than emitted,
                                which is a HONEST answer and still a no

    ORDER (bear-trap #25): jitted half FIRST, oracle last.
    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitXmutual);
define
    jmN;
    jmTicks;
    jmA code={
        if jmN > 0;
            jmTicks = jmTicks + 1;
            jmN = jmN - 1;
            jmB();
        };
    jmB code={
        if jmN > 0;
            jmTicks = jmTicks + 1;
            jmN = jmN - 1;
            jmA();
        };
    ;

jmN     = 4;
jmTicks = 0;
print "XM fire 1 setup : jmN =" jmN:;
testing(jmA);
print "XM fire 1 result: jmTicks =" jmTicks " (want 4)":;

jmN = 6;
print "XM fire 2 setup : jmN =" jmN " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "XM fire 2 result: jmTicks =" jmTicks " (want 10 = 4+6)":;

jmN     = 4;
jmTicks = 0;
jmA();
print "XM interpreted  : jmTicks =" jmTicks " (the oracle -- want 4)":;

print "XM SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
